  "Scaffolding Beam Ladders & Lattice Girders": "Scaffolding Beam Ladders & Lattice Girders",
  "Scaffolding Beam Ladders and Lattice Girders are structural spanning components manufactured from 48.3 mm high-yield steel tubing. Designed to bridge over wide openings, vehicular roadways, pedestrian thoroughfares, and roof voids where continuous ground-supported scaffolding is impractical.\n\nEngineered with full-penetration welding between chords and diagonal lattice bracing, conforming to BS 1139 and EN 12811 for high bending moment capacity and point load resistance.": "Scaffolding Beam Ladders and Lattice Girders are structural spanning components manufactured from 48.3 mm high-yield steel tubing. Designed to bridge over wide openings, vehicular roadways, pedestrian thoroughfares, and roof voids where continuous ground-supported scaffolding is impractical.\n\nEngineered with full-penetration welding between chords and diagonal lattice bracing, conforming to BS 1139 and EN 12811 for high bending moment capacity and point load resistance.",
  "Scaffolding Beam Ladders and Lattice Girders are structural spanning components manufactured from 48.3 mm high-yield steel tubing. Designed to bridge over wide openings, vehicular roadways, pedestrian thoroughfares, and roof voids where continuous ground-supported scaffolding is impractical. Engineered with full-penetration welding between chords and diagonal lattice bracing, conforming to BS 1139 and EN 12811 for high bending moment capacity and point load resistance.": "Scaffolding Beam Ladders and Lattice Girders are structural spanning components manufactured from 48.3 mm high-yield steel tubing. Designed to bridge over wide openings, vehicular roadways, pedestrian thoroughfares, and roof voids where continuous ground-supported scaffolding is impractical. Engineered with full-penetration welding between chords and diagonal lattice bracing, conforming to BS 1139 and EN 12811 for high bending moment capacity and point load resistance.",
  "Scaffolding Components & Accessories": "Scaffolding Components & Accessories",
  "Scaffolding components and accessories are used to assemble, support, access, protect, and stabilize scaffolding systems for safe construction and maintenance works. Every single component in a scaffold assembly has an indispensable engineering purpose—removing or incorrectly installing a single component affects the structural load transfer, worker safety, and stability of the entire scaffold structure.\n\nTianjin Decent International Trade Co., Ltd. supplies the complete inventory of 17 essential components and accessories manufactured from suitable high-strength steel or aluminum, with hot-dip galvanized or approved protective finishes as applicable.": "Scaffolding components and accessories are used to assemble, support, access, protect, and stabilize scaffolding systems for safe construction and maintenance works. Every single component in a scaffold assembly has an indispensable engineering purpose—removing or incorrectly installing a single component affects the structural load transfer, worker safety, and stability of the entire scaffold structure.\n\nTianjin Decent International Trade Co., Ltd. supplies the complete inventory of 17 essential components and accessories manufactured from suitable high-strength steel or aluminum, with hot-dip galvanized or approved protective finishes as applicable.",
  "Scaffolding components and accessories are used to assemble, support, access, protect, and stabilize scaffolding systems for safe construction and maintenance works. Every single component in a scaffold assembly has an indispensable engineering purpose—removing or incorrectly installing a single component affects the structural load transfer, worker safety, and stability of the entire scaffold structure. Tianjin Decent International Trade Co., Ltd. supplies the complete inventory of 17 essential components and accessories manufactured from suitable high-strength steel or aluminum, with hot-dip galvanized or approved protective finishes as applicable.": "Scaffolding components and accessories are used to assemble, support, access, protect, and stabilize scaffolding systems for safe construction and maintenance works. Every single component in a scaffold assembly has an indispensable engineering purpose—removing or incorrectly installing a single component affects the structural load transfer, worker safety, and stability of the entire scaffold structure. Tianjin Decent International Trade Co., Ltd. supplies the complete inventory of 17 essential components and accessories manufactured from suitable high-strength steel or aluminum, with hot-dip galvanized or approved protective finishes as applicable.",
  "Scaffolding couplers — Class B Certified": "Scaffolding couplers — Class B Certified",
  "Scaffolding couplers and tubes testing": "Scaffolding couplers and tubes testing",
  "Scaffolding Couplers supplied by Tianjin Decent International Trade Co., Ltd. are engineered for high slip resistance, rigidity, and rapid assembly across tube & coupler scaffolding, structural bracing, and modular falsework grids.\n\nManufactured from drop-forged high-tensile carbon steel and heavy pressed steel, equipped with Grade 8.8 forged T-bolts and flanged hex nuts. Conforming to EN 74-1 Class B and BS 1139, our comprehensive couplers range includes fixed right-angle double couplers, 360° universal swivel couplers, board retaining clamps (BRC), girder beam clamps, external sleeve couplers, and putlog single clamps with hot-dip galvanized or zinc electroplated finish.": "Scaffolding Couplers supplied by Tianjin Decent International Trade Co., Ltd. are engineered for high slip resistance, rigidity, and rapid assembly across tube & coupler scaffolding, structural bracing, and modular falsework grids.\n\nManufactured from drop-forged high-tensile carbon steel and heavy pressed steel, equipped with Grade 8.8 forged T-bolts and flanged hex nuts. Conforming to EN 74-1 Class B and BS 1139, our comprehensive couplers range includes fixed right-angle double couplers, 360° universal swivel couplers, board retaining clamps (BRC), girder beam clamps, external sleeve couplers, and putlog single clamps with hot-dip galvanized or zinc electroplated finish.",
